\begin{remark}
Of the $14$ solutions discovered by uniform-in-$m$ search with
$|m|>10^{8}$, seven of eight distinct fibers have $|n|>9000$ --- a strong
large-$|n|$ bias invisible to fixed-$n$ searches. The known range of $n$
grew from $[-1641,5118]$ to $[-14362,27949]$ over the course of the
computation.
\end{remark}

